    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0056" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg46"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lauchlin Currie to President Roosevelt </hi><anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d56-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-15">May 15, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Re: Owen Lattimore.</p>
                <p>I have received a cable from Madame Chiang for Owen Lattimore, asking him to
                    remain here for the next three or four months to emphasize to our people the
                    necessity of supporting China and regarding her as an equal partner in war and
                    peace.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lauch Currie</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d56-f1" n="3" type="source" xml:id="d56-f1-content">
                <p>Notation by President Roosevelt: “O.K. F.D.R.” Original returned to Mr. Currie.
                    Photostatic copy obtained from the Franklin D. Roosevelt Library, Hyde Park, N.
                    Y.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
